From 5aadda755bf098cc642dcc7e8352f4bc1c937132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:08:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ld/testsuite: widen the pr24511 xfail to all MicroBlaze
 targets

The test already xfails microblaze*-*-elf*, on the grounds given in its own
comment: "Most targets with their own scripts don't support init/fini_array
and thus don't define __init/fini_array_start."

MicroBlaze is such a target -- ld/scripttempl/elfmicroblaze.sc defines
neither symbol -- but the glob only covers *-elf triples, so the test fails
rather than xfails on microblaze-xilinx-rtems7 and any other MicroBlaze
triple.

Widen it to microblaze*-*-*.  ld/testsuite on microblaze-xilinx-rtems7 goes
from 478 passes and 1 unexpected failure to 479 and 0; on
microblaze-xilinx-elf the test was already XFAIL and is unaffected.

Providing the symbols in elfmicroblaze.sc would be the alternative fix, but
that changes what real links produce and is a separate question.

ld/
	* testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d: Widen the MicroBlaze xfail from
	microblaze*-*-elf* to microblaze*-*-*.
---
 ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d b/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d
index f77a43b9..ec7f584b 100644
--- a/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d
+++ b/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 # Most targets with their own scripts don't support init/fini_array and
 # thus don't define __init/fini_array_start.
 #xfail: avr-*-* cr16-*-* crx-*-* d10v-*-* d30v-*-* dlx-*-* ft32-*-* iq2000-*-*
-#xfail: m68hc1*-*-* mep-*-* microblaze*-*-elf* s12z-*-* v850-*-* visium-*-*
+#xfail: m68hc1*-*-* mep-*-* microblaze*-*-* s12z-*-* v850-*-* visium-*-*
 #xfail: xgate-*-* xstormy*-*-*
 # Some targets with their own scripts haven't kept up with elf.sc and
 # PROVIDE __init_array_start rather than using PROVIDE_HIDDEN.  These
